  "goodToKnow": "Das Moos is moss: Moos ansetzen (to gather moss, also figuratively). Colloquially, Moos means money, from Hebrew ma'oth via Yiddish: Ohne Moos nix los (no money, no fun) is a well-known saying. In Bavarian place names, Moos means a bog or moor: Dachauer Moos, Erdinger Moos (where Munich airport stands). Plural: die Moose."
